-- allium: 3
-- discovery.allium — how things are found and summarised: explore, search, indexers, insights, sitemap.
--
-- Scope: Every read path that lets a party *find* something they did not
--   navigate to directly, and every summary computed over a repository's
--   history. Search is always filtered to what the viewer may read; the read
--   rules themselves live in access.allium and are only referenced here.
--
-- Includes:
--   - The instance directory: explore pages for repositories, users,
--     organizations and code; the restrictions on them (sign-in requirement,
--     per-page disable switches, global code-unit disable).
--   - Repository search (web explore, profile/star/watch listings, JSON
--     pickers, REST `/repos/search`) with keyword, topic, language,
--     archived/fork/mirror/template/private facets, "relevant only", sorts.
--   - User and organization search (explore, REST `/users/search`, user
--     pickers), including the email-match privacy rule.
--   - Code search: per-repository, per-owner and instance-wide; the code
--     indexer (bleve / elasticsearch / zoekt), its eligibility rules
--     (repo kinds, include/exclude globs, vendored, size, binary), its
--     incremental refresh on pushes to the default branch, and the git-grep
--     fallback when no indexer is configured.
--   - The issue indexer (bleve / elasticsearch / meilisearch / db) and issue
--     search: keyword query language, filters, sort orders, per-repository
--     lists and cross-repository dashboards ("Issues", "Pull requests",
--     "Milestones"), and the REST `/repos/issues/search`.
--   - Re-index requests (site admin, per repository) and the scheduled full
--     issue-index rebuild.
--   - Repository insights: pulse (activity over a period), top committers,
--     contributors graph, code frequency, recent commits.
--   - User profile overview tabs (README from the `.profile` repository,
--     repositories, stars, watching, followers, following).
--   - Mention / assignee autocomplete candidates and the user picker.
--   - Topic search, sitemap (index + pages), robots policy, `?go-get=1`
--     import metadata.
--   - The miscellaneous REST surface: markup rendering (with the
--     sanitisation guarantee), version, gitignore / license / label
--     template catalogues.
--
-- Excludes:
--   - Who may read what (access.allium) — referenced through the local
--     predicates listed below.
--   - Storing language statistics (repositories.allium owns LanguageStat);
--     this module decides *when* they are recomputed, measures them, and
--     exposes the primary language as a search facet.
--   - Activity feeds, heatmaps, RSS/Atom, the home dashboard feed
--     (notifications.allium owns them); the profile "activity" tab is theirs.
--   - Organization home page and team/member listings (organizations.allium).
--   - Admin user/repo/org management lists (administration.allium) even
--     though they reuse the search machinery.
--   - Wiki content search (wiki.allium).
--   - NodeInfo / WebFinger (federation.allium); signing-key endpoints
--     (keys.allium); `/actions/run` (actions.allium); `/api/v1/settings/*`
--     (administration.allium).
--   - The detailed sanitiser allow-list and every markup renderer
--     (markdown extensions, org-mode, csv, asciicast, external renderers):
--     deferred to a markup specification; only the guarantee is kept here.
--   - Gitea-compatibility aliases: legacy `fuzzy=true` query flag, legacy
--     `DISABLE_SANITIZER`, the `gitea_codes` / `gitea_issues` index names,
--     index storage paths and connection strings (pure infrastructure).
--   - Search result highlighting/formatting and pagination link headers
--     (presentation).
--
-- Emits:
--   - LanguageStatsComputed(repository, commit_sha, sizes)
--       -- repositories replaces the repository's LanguageStat rows
--   - CodeIndexRefreshed(repository, commit_sha)
--       -- informational: the code index now reflects that default-branch commit
--   - IndexerStartupFailed(kind)
--       -- administration may record a SystemNotice
--   - CodeSearchAnswered(search), ContributorStatsGenerationStarted(repository, revision),
--     TemplateRead(client, template), IssueIndexRebuildStarted(service)
--       -- internal / informational
--
-- Reacts to:
--   - code/CommitsPushed(repository, branch_name, ...)   -- default-branch pushes
--       (including mirror syncs) refresh the code index and language statistics
--   - code/DefaultBranchChanged(repository, old_name, new_name, by)
--   - repositories/RepositoryCreated, RepositoryAdopted, RepositoryDeleted,
--     RepositoryVisibilityChanged (repository, doer)
--   - migrations/RepositoryMigrated(repository)
--   - issues/IssueOpened, IssueClosed, IssueReopened, IssueDeleted,
--     IssueTitleChanged, IssueContentChanged, IssueRefChanged,
--     IssueLabelsChanged, IssueLabelsCleared, IssueMilestoneChanged,
--     IssueAssigneeChanged, IssueCommentCreated, IssueCommentEdited,
--     IssueCommentDeleted
--   - pulls/PullRequestOpened(pull_request), PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger),
--     PullRequestAutoMerged(pull_request, merger), ReviewSubmitted(review),
--     ReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, reviewer),
--     ReviewRequestRemoved(pull_request, doer, reviewer)
--   - administration/IssueIndexRebuildDue()   -- the cron task (and "run now")
--
-- Black-box predicates. Qualified calls into sibling modules cannot yet be
-- simulated, so the predicates this module needs are named locally, each
-- delegating to its owner:
--   can_read_code(user?, repository)      -- access/can_read(user, repository, code)
--   can_read_issues(user?, repository)    -- access/can_read(user, repository, issues)
--   can_read_pulls(user?, repository)     -- access/can_read(user, repository, pull_requests)
--   can_read_releases(user?, repository)  -- access/can_read(user, repository, releases)
--   can_see_repository(user?, repository)   -- access/has_any_access
--   can_see_profile(viewer?, user)          -- access/can_see_profile
--   can_see_owner(viewer?, owner)           -- access/can_see_owner_user
--   is_org_member(user, organization)       -- organizations membership
--   listable_account(user, viewer?)         -- user-directory visibility: site admins see all;
--       signed-in users see public and limited accounts (restricted users: none), organizations
--       they belong to, and themselves; anonymous visitors see public accounts only
--   listable_organization(org, viewer?)     -- same rule applied to organizations
-- Singletons are reached through accessors: directory(), code_search_service(),
-- issue_index_service(). Other free-standing calls are query black boxes whose
-- meaning is given in the comment of the rule that uses them.

use "./accounts.allium" as accounts
use "./organizations.allium" as organizations
use "./repositories.allium" as repositories
use "./access.allium" as access
use "./code.allium" as code
use "./issues.allium" as issues
use "./pulls.allium" as pulls
use "./releases.allium" as releases
use "./migrations.allium" as migrations
use "./projects.allium" as projects
use "./administration.allium" as administration

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- One line of a code search hit, with its line number. The matched range is
-- highlighted; one line of context is shown either side of a match.
value CodeHitLine {
    number: Integer
    text: String
}

-- Aggregate git statistics over a period on one branch.
-- from: modules/git/repo_stats.go:20
value CodeActivity {
    author_count: Integer
    commit_count: Integer
    commit_count_all_branches: Integer
    changed_files: Integer
    additions: Integer
    deletions: Integer
}

-- A committer in the "top authors" list. A committer whose email matches no
-- account is shown by commit name only, with the ghost avatar.
-- from: models/activities/repo_activity.go:23
value ActivityAuthor {
    name: String
    account: accounts/User?
    commits: Integer
}

-- One week of a contributor's history (weeks start on Sunday).
-- from: services/repository/contributors_graph.go:39
value ContributorWeek {
    week_start: Timestamp
    additions: Integer
    deletions: Integer
    commits: Integer
}

-- One contributor series in the contributors graph. Commits are attributed
-- to an account by author email (primary or any verified address); unknown
-- emails stay as a name-only series. The special series "total" is the sum.
value ContributorSeries {
    name: String
    account: accounts/User?
    total_commits: Integer
    weeks: List<ContributorWeek>
}

-- A parsed term of the issue search query language (see IssueSearch).
-- from: modules/indexer/issues/internal/qstring.go:27
value QueryToken {
    term: String
    occurrence: must | should | must_not
    exact: Boolean        -- "quoted phrase" (no fuzzy matching)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: models/repo/search.go:36
enum RepoSortOrder {
    newest | oldest
    | recent_update | least_update
    | alphabetically | reverse_alphabetically
    | size | reverse_size
    | git_size | reverse_git_size
    | lfs_size | reverse_lfs_size
    | most_stars | fewest_stars
    | most_forks | fewest_forks
}

-- Only newest/oldest/alphabetically/reverse_alphabetically are offered on the
-- explore users/organizations pages; the rest are admin listing orders.
-- from: routers/web/explore/user.go:155
enum UserSortOrder {
    newest | oldest
    | alphabetically | reverse_alphabetically
    | recent_update | least_update
    | last_login | reverse_last_login
}

-- Narrowing facets for a repository search. Opposite pairs are mutually
-- exclusive; absent from the set means "either".
-- from: models/repo/repo_list.go:130
enum RepoFacet {
    archived | not_archived
    | fork | not_fork
    | mirror | not_mirror
    | template | not_template
    | private | public
    | collaborative_only    -- repos the subject does not own but has access to
    | owned_only            -- API `exclusive`
    | topic_only            -- keyword matches topic names exactly
    | relevant_only         -- hide forks unless asked; require description, topic or avatar; hide empty
}

-- What a repository listing is about.
enum RepoSearchScope {
    explore                -- everything the viewer can read
    | owned_by             -- repositories of `subject` (profile "Repositories" tab, API `uid`)
    | starred_by           -- profile "Stars" tab, API `starredBy`
    | watched_by           -- profile "Watching" tab
}

enum UserSearchScope {
    explore                -- /explore/users
    | api                  -- REST /users/search (also matches email)
    | picker               -- /user/search_candidates (active users only)
}

-- Lifecycle of an indexer backend.
enum BackendStatus { starting | ready | unavailable }

-- Lifecycle of a queued indexing job.
enum JobStatus { queued | completed | skipped }

-- Lifecycle of a job that is never skipped.
enum DrainStatus { queued | drained }

enum CodeIndexerKind { bleve | elasticsearch | zoekt }

enum IssueIndexerKind { bleve | elasticsearch | meilisearch | db }

-- Which repository kinds the code indexer covers (REPO_INDEXER_REPO_TYPES).
enum RepoKindForIndex { sources | forks | mirrors | templates }

-- exact: the phrase as typed; union: any of the words; fuzzy: approximate
-- word match (only when enabled, otherwise downgraded to union); regexp:
-- only with the git-grep fallback.
-- from: routers/web/repo/search.go:24
enum CodeSearchMode { exact | union | fuzzy | regexp }

enum CodeSearchScope { instance | owner | repository }

-- from: modules/indexer/issues/internal/model.go:140
enum IssueSortOrder {
    relevance
    | latest | oldest
    | recent_update | least_update
    | most_comment | least_comment
    | near_due_date | far_due_date
}

enum IssueStateFilter { open | closed | all }

enum IssueKindFilter { issues_only | pulls_only | both }

-- How the viewer is involved; `your_repositories` means "in repositories I
-- own or collaborate on", `all` means no involvement filter.
-- from: routers/web/user/home.go:423
enum InvolvementFilter {
    all
    | your_repositories
    | created_by
    | assigned
    | mentioned
    | review_requested
    | reviewed_by
}

enum IssueSearchScope {
    repository             -- one repository's issue or PR list
    | dashboard            -- /issues, /pulls for the signed-in user
    | organization         -- /org/{org}/issues|pulls (optionally one team)
    | api                  -- REST /repos/issues/search
}

-- from: routers/web/repo/activity.go:31
enum ActivityPeriod { daily | halfweekly | weekly | monthly | quarterly | semiyearly | yearly }

-- from: routers/web/user/profile.go:173
enum ProfileTab { overview | repositories | stars | watching | followers | following }

enum SitemapSection { users | repositories }

-- from: routers/common/markup.go:44
enum MarkupMode {
    markdown               -- raw markdown, no repository metas
    | comment              -- markdown as an issue comment (hard line breaks, issue refs)
    | gfm                  -- markdown as a document
    | file                 -- pick renderer by `file_path` extension
}

-- How output of external (non-built-in) renderers is delivered.
enum RenderContentMode { sanitized | no_sanitizer | iframe }

enum TemplateKind { gitignore | license | label_set }

enum CloneProtocol { https | ssh }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The instance's public directory: explore area, sitemap, robots policy and
-- the public version string. A single instance exists, reached through the
-- black-box accessor `directory()`. Its switches are initialised from config
-- at start-up.
-- from: modules/setting/service.go:104
entity Directory {
    require_signin_view: Boolean              -- [service] REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW (whole instance)
    explore_require_signin: Boolean           -- [service.explore] REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW
    users_page_disabled: Boolean
    organizations_page_disabled: Boolean
    code_page_disabled: Boolean
    code_unit_globally_disabled: Boolean      -- repositories: code unit disabled instance-wide
    sitemap_enabled: Boolean
    milestones_dashboard_enabled: Boolean
    custom_robots_policy: String?             -- operator-supplied robots policy file
    version: String                           -- running application version

    -- Derived
    explore_requires_signin: require_signin_view or explore_require_signin
    robots_policy: custom_robots_policy ?? default_robots_policy()
}

-- The code indexer. Only one exists (`code_search_service()`). When
-- `enabled` is false, repository code search falls back to git grep and the
-- instance/owner code search pages are unavailable.
-- from: modules/indexer/code/indexer.go:111
entity CodeSearchService {
    enabled: Boolean                          -- REPO_INDEXER_ENABLED
    kind: CodeIndexerKind
    fuzzy_enabled: Boolean                    -- REPO_INDEXER_FUZZY_ENABLED
    status: BackendStatus
    started_at: Timestamp

    entries: CodeIndexEntry with service = this

    transitions status {
        starting -> ready
        starting -> unavailable
        ready -> unavailable
        unavailable -> ready
    }

    -- Derived
    is_available: enabled and status = ready
}

-- The issue indexer. Always present (`issue_index_service()`); the `db`
-- kind answers keyword searches straight from the issue store.
-- from: modules/indexer/issues/indexer.go:65
entity IssueIndexService {
    kind: IssueIndexerKind
    status: BackendStatus
    started_at: Timestamp
    last_full_rebuild_at: Timestamp?

    documents: IssueIndexDocument with service = this

    transitions status {
        starting -> ready
        starting -> unavailable
        ready -> unavailable
        unavailable -> ready
    }

    -- Derived
    is_available: status = ready
}

-- The code index's knowledge of one repository: which default-branch commit
-- it reflects. A repository with no entry has never been indexed.
-- from: models/repo/repo_indexer.go:27
entity CodeIndexEntry {
    service: CodeSearchService
    repository: repositories/Repository
    commit_sha: String
    indexed_at: Timestamp

    documents: CodeIndexDocument with entry = this
}

-- One indexed file at the entry's commit. Binary (non-text) files keep their
-- path searchable but carry no content.
-- from: modules/indexer/code/bleve/bleve.go:143
entity CodeIndexDocument {
    entry: CodeIndexEntry
    path: String
    language: String?
    content_indexed: Boolean
    updated_at: Timestamp
}

-- The last default-branch commit for which language statistics were
-- computed. Recomputing for the same commit is skipped.
-- from: modules/indexer/stats/db.go:35
entity LanguageStatsMark {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    commit_sha: String
}

-- The searchable projection of one issue or pull request. Every field below
-- is refreshed whenever the issue, its comments, labels, assignees,
-- milestone, project, reviews or the repository's visibility change.
-- from: modules/indexer/issues/internal/model.go:13
entity IssueIndexDocument {
    service: IssueIndexService
    issue: issues/Issue
    repository: repositories/Repository
    is_public: Boolean                        -- repository is not private
    title: String
    content: String
    comments: List<String>                    -- non-empty conversation comments
    is_pull: Boolean
    is_closed: Boolean
    labels: Set<issues/Label>
    milestone: issues/Milestone?
    project: projects/Project?
    project_column: projects/ProjectColumn?
    poster: accounts/User
    assignees: Set<accounts/User>
    mentioned: Set<accounts/User>
    reviewed_by: Set<accounts/User>
    review_requested: Set<accounts/User>
    subscribers: Set<accounts/User>
    created_at: Timestamp
    updated_at: Timestamp
    deadline: Timestamp?
    comment_count: Integer
}

-- Units of indexing work. Each queue is unique: at most one pending job per
-- target. Jobs whose processing fails are retried until they succeed; a job
-- is never silently dropped.

-- Bring one repository's code index up to its default-branch head.
-- from: modules/indexer/code/indexer.go:134
entity CodeIndexJob {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    status: JobStatus
    queued_at: Timestamp

    transitions status {
        queued -> completed
        queued -> skipped
        terminal: completed, skipped
    }
}

-- Recompute one repository's language statistics.
-- from: modules/indexer/stats/queue.go
entity LanguageStatsJob {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    status: JobStatus
    queued_at: Timestamp

    transitions status {
        queued -> completed
        queued -> skipped
        terminal: completed, skipped
    }
}

-- Refresh or remove one issue's document.
-- from: modules/indexer/issues/indexer.go:173
entity IssueIndexJob {
    issue: issues/Issue
    action: index | remove
    status: DrainStatus
    queued_at: Timestamp

    transitions status {
        queued -> drained
        terminal: drained
    }
}

-- Re-queue or remove every issue document of a repository.
-- from: modules/indexer/issues/util.go:132
entity RepositoryIssuesJob {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    action: reindex | remove
    status: DrainStatus
    queued_at: Timestamp

    transitions status {
        queued -> drained
        terminal: drained
    }
}

-- A repository listing request and its answer.
-- from: routers/web/explore/repo.go:37
entity RepositorySearch {
    viewer: accounts/User?
    scope: RepoSearchScope
    subject: accounts/User?                   -- owner / starrer / watcher for non-explore scopes
    keyword: String
    language: String?                         -- primary language filter
    facets: Set<RepoFacet>
    include_description: Boolean
    sort: RepoSortOrder
    page: Integer
    page_size: Integer
    results: List<repositories/Repository>
    total: Integer
    searched_at: Timestamp
}

-- A user directory/picker request.
-- from: models/user/search.go:20
entity UserSearch {
    viewer: accounts/User?
    scope: UserSearchScope
    keyword: String
    sort: UserSortOrder
    match_email: Boolean
    page_size: Integer
    results: List<accounts/User>
    total: Integer
}

-- An organization directory request.
-- from: routers/web/explore/org.go:15
entity OrganizationSearch {
    viewer: accounts/User?
    keyword: String
    sort: UserSortOrder
    page_size: Integer
    results: List<organizations/Organization>
    total: Integer
}

-- A code search and its hits.
-- from: routers/web/explore/code.go:25
entity CodeSearch {
    viewer: accounts/User?
    scope: CodeSearchScope
    owner: accounts/User?                     -- scope = owner
    repository: repositories/Repository?      -- scope = repository
    ref_name: String?                         -- git-grep fallback only: branch or tag searched (null = default branch)
    keyword: String
    language: String?
    path: String?                             -- restrict to paths containing this
    requested_mode: CodeSearchMode
    effective_mode: CodeSearchMode
    used_index: Boolean                       -- false = git grep fallback
    index_unavailable: Boolean                -- shown as a warning, results may be empty
    total: Integer
    hits: CodeSearchHit with search = this
    languages: List<String>                   -- language facet counts of the hits
}

-- from: modules/indexer/code/internal/model.go:66
entity CodeSearchHit {
    search: CodeSearch
    repository: repositories/Repository
    path: String
    commit_sha: String
    language: String?
    lines: List<CodeHitLine>
}

-- An issue/pull-request listing or search.
-- from: routers/web/user/home.go:374
entity IssueSearch {
    viewer: accounts/User?
    scope: IssueSearchScope
    repository: repositories/Repository?          -- scope = repository
    context_owner: accounts/User?                 -- dashboard user
    context_org: organizations/Organization?      -- scope = organization
    context_team: organizations/Team?
    keyword: String
    tokens: List<QueryToken>
    kind: IssueKindFilter
    state: IssueStateFilter
    involvement: InvolvementFilter
    labels: Set<issues/Label>?                    -- must carry all of these
    excluded_labels: Set<issues/Label>?
    no_label_only: Boolean
    milestones: Set<issues/Milestone>?
    no_milestone_only: Boolean
    project: projects/Project?
    poster: accounts/User?
    assignee: accounts/User?
    no_assignee_only: Boolean
    mentioned: accounts/User?
    review_requested_of: accounts/User?
    reviewed_by: accounts/User?
    updated_after: Timestamp?
    updated_before: Timestamp?
    include_all_public: Boolean                   -- also search public repos the viewer has no explicit role in
    searchable_repositories: Set<repositories/Repository>
    sort: IssueSortOrder
    page: Integer
    page_size: Integer
    used_index: Boolean                           -- false when keyword is empty (listing from the store)
    index_unavailable: Boolean
    results: List<issues/Issue>
    open_count: Integer
    closed_count: Integer
}

-- The cross-repository milestones overview (/milestones).
-- from: routers/web/user/home.go:145
entity MilestoneOverview {
    viewer: accounts/User
    context_org: organizations/Organization?
    keyword: String
    show_closed: Boolean
    repositories: Set<repositories/Repository>
    milestones: List<issues/Milestone>
}

-- Topic search for pickers and the API.
-- from: models/repo/topic.go:145
entity TopicSearch {
    keyword: String
    results: List<repositories/Topic>         -- most-used first
}

-- Autocomplete candidates offered while composing in a repository.
-- from: routers/web/repo/issue.go:3793
entity MentionCandidates {
    viewer: accounts/User
    repository: repositories/Repository
    issue: issues/Issue?
    users: Set<accounts/User>
    teams: Set<organizations/Team>
}

-- A repository pulse for a period.
-- from: models/activities/repo_activity.go:32
entity ActivityReport {
    viewer: accounts/User?
    repository: repositories/Repository
    period: ActivityPeriod
    from: Timestamp
    until: Timestamp
    includes_releases: Boolean
    includes_issues: Boolean
    includes_pulls: Boolean
    includes_code: Boolean
    merged_pulls: Set<pulls/PullRequest>
    opened_pulls: Set<pulls/PullRequest>
    opened_issues: Set<issues/Issue>
    closed_issues: Set<issues/Issue>
    unresolved_issues: Set<issues/Issue>
    published_releases: Set<releases/Release>
    code: CodeActivity?
    top_authors: List<ActivityAuthor>

    -- Derived
    active_pull_count: merged_pulls.count + opened_pulls.count
    active_issue_count: opened_issues.count + closed_issues.count
}

-- Contributor statistics for one revision. Expensive: generated in the
-- background on first request, served while fresh, then discarded.
-- from: services/repository/contributors_graph.go:84
entity ContributorStats {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    revision: String
    status: generating | ready | failed
    requested_at: Timestamp
    series: List<ContributorSeries> when status = ready
    generated_at: Timestamp when status = ready
    expires_at: Timestamp when status = ready | failed

    transitions status {
        generating -> ready
        generating -> failed
        terminal: ready, failed
    }
}

-- A profile page view.
-- from: routers/web/user/profile.go:60
entity ProfileView {
    viewer: accounts/User?
    subject: accounts/User
    requested_tab: ProfileTab
    tab: ProfileTab
    has_profile_readme: Boolean
    shows_private: Boolean                     -- viewer is the subject or a site admin
    repositories: List<repositories/Repository>
    people: List<accounts/User>                -- followers / following tabs
    total: Integer
}

-- A sitemap document.
-- from: routers/web/home.go:92
entity SitemapDocument {
    is_index: Boolean
    section: SitemapSection?
    page: Integer
    entry_count: Integer
}

-- The answer to `?go-get=1` on any `/{owner}/{repo}...` path.
-- from: routers/web/goget.go:20
entity GoImportAnswer {
    owner_name: String
    repo_name: String
    import_path: String                        -- host[/subpath]/owner/repo (".git" suffix trimmed)
    clone_url: String
    source_branch: String
    insecure_hint: Boolean                     -- instance served over plain HTTP
}

-- A markup rendering request (REST /markup, /markdown, /markdown/raw and the
-- web preview).
-- from: routers/common/markup.go:28
entity MarkupRendering {
    requester: accounts/User
    mode: MarkupMode
    text: String
    context_path: String?
    file_path: String?
    is_wiki: Boolean
    repository: repositories/Repository?
    html: String
}

-- A built-in template offered at repository creation and through the API.
-- from: routers/api/v1/misc/gitignore.go:17
entity TemplateFile {
    kind: TemplateKind
    name: String
    content: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [service] / [service.explore]
    require_signin_view: Boolean = false
    explore_require_signin_view: Boolean = false
    explore_disable_users_page: Boolean = false
    explore_disable_organizations_page: Boolean = false
    explore_disable_code_page: Boolean = false
    show_milestones_dashboard_page: Boolean = true

    -- [other]
    enable_sitemap: Boolean = true

    -- [ui]
    explore_page_size: Integer = 20                    -- EXPLORE_PAGING_NUM
    sitemap_page_size: Integer = 20                    -- SITEMAP_PAGING_NUM
    issue_page_size: Integer = 20                      -- ISSUE_PAGING_NUM
    code_search_page_size: Integer = 20                -- REPO_SEARCH_PAGING_NUM
    picker_page_size: Integer = 20                     -- MEMBERS_PAGING_NUM
    profile_repo_page_size: Integer = 15               -- [ui.user] REPO_PAGING_NUM
    explore_default_sort: RepoSortOrder = recent_update -- EXPLORE_PAGING_DEFAULT_SORT
    only_show_relevant_repos: Boolean = false          -- ONLY_SHOW_RELEVANT_REPOS
    search_repo_description: Boolean = true           -- SEARCH_REPO_DESCRIPTION
    show_user_email: Boolean = true                    -- SHOW_USER_EMAIL

    -- [api]
    api_default_page_size: Integer = 30
    api_max_page_size: Integer = 50

    -- [indexer] code
    repo_indexer_enabled: Boolean = false
    repo_indexer_kind: CodeIndexerKind = bleve
    repo_indexer_repo_types: Set<RepoKindForIndex> = { sources, forks, mirrors, templates }
    repo_indexer_fuzzy_enabled: Boolean = false
    repo_indexer_include: String = ""                   -- comma-separated globs, lower-cased
    repo_indexer_exclude: String = ""
    repo_indexer_exclude_vendored: Boolean = true
    max_indexer_file_size: Integer = 1048576            -- bytes; larger files are not indexed

    -- [indexer] issues
    issue_indexer_kind: IssueIndexerKind = bleve
    indexer_startup_timeout: Duration = 30.seconds      -- STARTUP_TIMEOUT; 0 disables

    -- [cron.rebuild_issue_indexer]
    rebuild_issue_indexer_enabled: Boolean = false
    rebuild_issue_indexer_interval: Duration = 365.days -- schedule @annually

    -- git-grep fallback (fixed by Forgejo, not app.ini)
    grep_max_result_files: Integer = 50
    grep_max_matches_per_file: Integer = 20
    grep_context_lines: Integer = 1

    -- insights
    activity_top_authors: Integer = 10
    contributor_stats_ttl: Duration = 16.hours          -- [cache] ITEM_TTL

    -- [repository]
    go_get_clone_url_protocol: CloneProtocol = https    -- GO_GET_CLONE_URL_PROTOCOL
    default_branch_name: String = "main"                -- [repository] DEFAULT_BRANCH

    -- [markup]
    render_content_mode: RenderContentMode = sanitized  -- per external renderer RENDER_CONTENT_MODE
    custom_url_schemes: String = ""                     -- [markdown] CUSTOM_URL_SCHEMES
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Explore: repositories
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The single repository-listing operation behind explore, profile tabs, the
-- JSON picker and REST /repos/search.
--
-- Keyword: comma-separated alternatives; each alternative matches a
-- repository whose name contains it, or whose topic name contains it, or
-- (when include_description) whose description contains it. A keyword of
-- the form "owner/name" also matches by owner and name, and such results
-- are ordered owner-matches first. With the topic_only facet an alternative
-- must equal a topic name exactly.
-- from: routers/web/explore/repo.go:37
rule ViewerSearchesRepositories {
    when: ViewerSearchesRepositories(viewer, scope, subject, keyword, language, facets, sort)
    let dir = directory()
    requires: viewer != null or not (dir.require_signin_view or dir.explore_require_signin)
    requires: scope = explore or subject != null
    let found = repository_search(viewer, scope, subject, keyword, language, facets, sort)
    ensures: RepositorySearch.created(
        viewer: viewer,
        scope: scope,
        subject: subject,
        keyword: keyword,
        language: language,
        facets: facets,
        include_description: config.search_repo_description,
        sort: sort,
        page: 1,
        page_size: config.explore_page_size,
        results: found,
        total: repository_search_total(viewer, scope, subject, keyword, language, facets),
        searched_at: now
    )
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /explore/repos (q, sort, topic, language, archived, fork,
        --   mirror, template, private, only_show_relevant, page);
        --   GET /{user}?tab=repositories|stars|watching (same filters);
        --   GET /repo/search (JSON picker: q, uid, priority_owner_id,
        --   team_id, topic, private, starredBy, includeDesc, template,
        --   exclusive, mode=source|fork|mirror|collaborative, archived).
        -- API: GET /api/v1/repos/search (same as the JSON picker, plus
        --   sort=alpha|created|updated|size|git_size|lfs_size|id|stars|forks
        --   and order=asc|desc). An unknown mode, sort or order is rejected.
        -- `priority_owner_id` orders that owner's repositories first;
        -- `team_id` restricts to one team's repositories.
        -- An unknown `sort` on web pages falls back to recent_update; an
        -- empty one uses config.explore_default_sort.
        -- Page sizes: explore = explore_page_size, profile tabs =
        -- profile_repo_page_size, API = limit capped at api_max_page_size.
        -- The explore page adds relevant_only by default when
        -- config.only_show_relevant_repos is on (overridable per request).
        -- The JSON picker (/repo/search) requires sign-in.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Explore: users and organizations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Keyword matches (case-insensitively) the login name or full name, and in
-- the API scope also the email address — but an email only matches when it
-- is not kept private, or belongs to the viewer, or the viewer is a site
-- admin. Only individual (and remote) accounts are listed; the explore and
-- picker scopes list only activated accounts.
-- from: routers/web/explore/user.go:121
rule ViewerSearchesUsers {
    when: ViewerSearchesUsers(viewer, scope, keyword, sort)
    let dir = directory()
    requires: viewer != null or not (dir.require_signin_view or dir.explore_require_signin)
    requires: scope != explore or not dir.users_page_disabled
    requires: scope != api or not dir.users_page_disabled
    requires: scope = api or sort in { newest, oldest, alphabetically, reverse_alphabetically }
    requires: not contains_nul(keyword)
    let found = user_search(viewer, scope, keyword, sort)
    ensures: UserSearch.created(
        viewer: viewer,
        scope: scope,
        keyword: keyword,
        sort: sort,
        match_email: scope = api,
        page_size: config.explore_page_size,
        results: found,
        total: user_search_total(viewer, scope, keyword)
    )
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /explore/users (q, sort, page; sitemap pages reuse it);
        --   GET /user/search_candidates (q) — picker for collaborators,
        --   team members, assignees; page size picker_page_size.
        -- API: GET /api/v1/users/search (q, uid, sort, page, limit). The
        --   pseudo-ids of the ghost user and the actions bot answer with that
        --   single pseudo-account. A token restricted to public resources
        --   lists only public accounts.
        -- When the users page is disabled the API search answers "not found".
        -- An unsupported sort on the explore page is "not found".
}

-- Anonymous visitors see only public organizations; signed-in users also
-- see limited ones and private ones they belong to; restricted users see
-- only organizations they belong to; site admins see all.
-- from: routers/web/explore/org.go:15
rule ViewerExploresOrganizations {
    when: ViewerExploresOrganizations(viewer, keyword, sort)
    let dir = directory()
    requires: viewer != null or not (dir.require_signin_view or dir.explore_require_signin)
    requires: not dir.organizations_page_disabled
    requires: sort in { newest, oldest, alphabetically, reverse_alphabetically }
    let found = organization_search(viewer, keyword, sort)
    ensures: OrganizationSearch.created(
        viewer: viewer,
        keyword: keyword,
        sort: sort,
        page_size: config.explore_page_size,
        results: found,
        total: organization_search_total(viewer, keyword)
    )
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /explore/organizations (q, sort, page). A disabled page
        -- redirects to /explore/repos.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Topics, templates, version
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Topic names containing the keyword, most-used first.
-- from: routers/web/explore/topic.go:16
rule ClientSearchesTopics {
    when: ClientSearchesTopics(client, keyword)
    let dir = directory()
    requires: client != null or not (dir.require_signin_view or dir.explore_require_signin)
    ensures: TopicSearch.created(keyword: keyword, results: topic_search(keyword))
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /explore/topics/search (q, page, limit).
        -- API: GET /api/v1/topics/search (q, page, limit).
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/misc/gitignore.go:30
rule ClientReadsTemplate {
    when: ClientReadsTemplate(client, kind, name)
    let template = TemplateFile{kind: kind, name: name}
    requires: exists template
    ensures: TemplateRead(client: client, template: template)
    @guidance
        -- API: GET /gitignore/templates, /gitignore/templates/{name},
        --   /licenses, /licenses/{name}, /label/templates,
        --   /label/templates/{name}. Listings are public; operator-supplied
        --   custom templates override built-in ones of the same name.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Code search
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Instance-wide code search across every repository whose code the viewer
-- can read (site admins: all repositories).
-- from: routers/web/explore/code.go:25
rule ViewerSearchesAllCode {
    when: ViewerSearchesAllCode(viewer, keyword, language, path, mode)
    let dir = directory()
    let service = code_search_service()
    requires: viewer != null or not (dir.require_signin_view or dir.explore_require_signin)
    requires: service.enabled
    requires: not dir.code_page_disabled
    requires: not dir.code_unit_globally_disabled
    requires: keyword != ""
    ensures:
        let search = CodeSearch.created(
            viewer: viewer,
            scope: instance,
            keyword: keyword,
            language: language,
            path: path,
            requested_mode: mode,
            effective_mode: mode,
            used_index: true,
            index_unavailable: service.status != ready,
            total: code_search_total(viewer, null, null, keyword, language, path, mode),
            languages: code_search_languages(viewer, null, null, keyword, mode)
        )
        if mode = regexp or (mode = fuzzy and not service.fuzzy_enabled):
            search.effective_mode = union
        CodeSearchAnswered(search: search)
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /explore/code (q, l, path, mode=exact|union|fuzzy, page).
        -- Disabled page or no indexer: redirect to /explore/repos.
        -- Hits of repositories deleted since indexing are dropped.
        -- An empty keyword shows the empty search form (no search).
}

-- Code search across one owner's repositories (profile "Code" tab).
-- from: routers/web/user/code.go:24
rule ViewerSearchesOwnerCode {
    when: ViewerSearchesOwnerCode(viewer, owner, keyword, language, path, mode)
    let service = code_search_service()
    requires: service.enabled
    requires: can_see_owner(viewer, owner)
    requires: keyword != ""
    ensures:
        let search = CodeSearch.created(
            viewer: viewer,
            scope: owner,
            owner: owner,
            keyword: keyword,
            language: language,
            path: path,
            requested_mode: mode,
            effective_mode: mode,
            used_index: true,
            index_unavailable: service.status != ready,
            total: code_search_total(viewer, owner, null, keyword, language, path, mode),
            languages: code_search_languages(viewer, owner, null, keyword, mode)
        )
        if mode = regexp or (mode = fuzzy and not service.fuzzy_enabled):
            search.effective_mode = union
        CodeSearchAnswered(search: search)
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{owner}/-/code (q, l, path, mode, page). Without an
        -- indexer this page redirects to the owner's profile.
}

-- Code search in one repository using the index.
-- from: routers/web/repo/search.go:65
rule ReaderSearchesRepositoryCodeIndexed {
    when: ReaderSearchesRepositoryCode(viewer, repository, ref_name, keyword, path, mode)
    let service = code_search_service()
    requires: can_read_code(viewer, repository)
    requires: service.enabled
    requires: keyword != ""
    ensures:
        let search = CodeSearch.created(
            viewer: viewer,
            scope: repository,
            repository: repository,
            keyword: keyword,
            path: path,
            requested_mode: mode,
            effective_mode: mode,
            used_index: true,
            index_unavailable: service.status != ready,
            total: code_search_total(viewer, null, repository, keyword, null, path, mode),
            languages: code_search_languages(viewer, null, repository, keyword, mode)
        )
        if mode = regexp or (mode = fuzzy and not service.fuzzy_enabled):
            search.effective_mode = union
        CodeSearchAnswered(search: search)
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{owner}/{repo}/search (q, l, path, mode, page). The index
        -- only knows the default branch, so `ref_name` is ignored here.
}

-- Code search in one repository without an index: git grep over the chosen
-- branch or tag (default branch when none is chosen). Case-insensitive.
-- Binary files are skipped. At most grep_max_result_files files and
-- grep_max_matches_per_file matches per file are reported, with
-- grep_context_lines lines of context. Global include/exclude patterns
-- still apply; when both a global include pattern and a `path` are given,
-- only paths satisfying both are searched. Fuzzy is not offered; regexp is.
-- from: routers/web/repo/search.go:134
rule ReaderSearchesRepositoryCodeByGrep {
    when: ReaderSearchesRepositoryCode(viewer, repository, ref_name, keyword, path, mode)
    let service = code_search_service()
    requires: can_read_code(viewer, repository)
    requires: not service.enabled
    requires: keyword != ""
    ensures:
        let search = CodeSearch.created(
            viewer: viewer,
            scope: repository,
            repository: repository,
            ref_name: ref_name,
            keyword: keyword,
            path: path,
            requested_mode: mode,
            effective_mode: mode,
            used_index: false,
            index_unavailable: false,
            total: grep_total(repository, ref_name, keyword, path, mode),
            languages: []
        )
        if mode = fuzzy:
            search.effective_mode = exact
        CodeSearchAnswered(search: search)
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{owner}/{repo}/search, /search/branch/{branch},
        --   /search/tag/{tag} (the latter two only exist without an indexer).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Code index maintenance
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: modules/indexer/code/indexer.go:111
rule CodeIndexerStarts {
    when: CodeIndexerStartupCompleted(service, index_was_empty)
    requires: service.status = starting
    ensures: service.status = ready
    ensures:
        if index_was_empty:
            for repository in all_repositories():
                CodeIndexRefreshRequested(repository: repository)
    @guidance
        -- A freshly created index is populated by queueing every existing
        -- repository (newest first), after forgetting any recorded index
        -- marks. Repositories created meanwhile are queued by their own events.
}

-- The indexer must become ready within the startup timeout; otherwise the
-- instance refuses to run with a half-initialised index.
-- from: modules/indexer/code/indexer.go:264
rule CodeIndexerStartupTimesOut {
    when: service: CodeSearchService.started_at + config.indexer_startup_timeout <= now
    requires: service.status = starting
    requires: service.enabled
    ensures: service.status = unavailable
    ensures: IndexerStartupFailed(kind: service.kind)
    @guidance
        -- Forgejo terminates the process here. A rebuild may instead keep
        -- serving with code search unavailable; see open questions.
}

-- from: modules/indexer/code/indexer.go:298
rule CodeIndexerBecomesUnreachable {
    when: CodeIndexerHealthChanged(service, reachable)
    requires: service.status = ready
    requires: not reachable
    ensures: service.status = unavailable
}

rule CodeIndexerRecovers {
    when: CodeIndexerHealthChanged(service, reachable)
    requires: service.status = unavailable
    requires: reachable
    ensures: service.status = ready
}

-- A push to the default branch (direct or via mirror sync) refreshes the
-- code index and language statistics. Pushes to other branches or tags
-- refresh language statistics only if they moved the default branch
-- (they do not).
-- from: services/indexer/notify.go:117
rule DefaultBranchPushRefreshesIndexes {
    when: code/CommitsPushed(repository, branch_name, pusher, old_sha, new_sha, is_force)
    requires: branch_name = repository.default_branch
    requires: new_sha != null
    ensures: CodeIndexRefreshRequested(repository: repository)
    ensures: LanguageStatsRefreshQueued(repository: repository)
}

-- from: services/indexer/notify.go:155
rule DefaultBranchChangeRefreshesIndexes {
    when: code/DefaultBranchChanged(repository, old_name, new_name, by)
    requires: not repository.is_empty
    ensures: CodeIndexRefreshRequested(repository: repository)
    ensures: LanguageStatsRefreshQueued(repository: repository)
}

-- from: services/indexer/notify.go:93
rule MigratedRepositoryIsIndexed {
    when: migrations/RepositoryMigrated(repository)
    ensures:
        if not repository.is_empty:
            CodeIndexRefreshRequested(repository: repository)
    ensures: LanguageStatsRefreshQueued(repository: repository)
    ensures: RepositoryIssuesReindexRequested(repository: repository)
}

-- Adopting unadopted repositories on disk behaves like a migration.
-- from: services/indexer/notify.go:32
rule AdoptedRepositoryIsIndexed {
    when: repositories/RepositoryAdopted(repository, doer)
    ensures:
        if not repository.is_empty:
            CodeIndexRefreshRequested(repository: repository)
    ensures: LanguageStatsRefreshQueued(repository: repository)
    ensures: RepositoryIssuesReindexRequested(repository: repository)
}

-- Deleting a repository removes all its code and issue documents.
-- from: services/indexer/notify.go:80
rule DeletedRepositoryLeavesIndexes {
    when: repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)
    let entry = CodeIndexEntry{repository: repository}
    ensures:
        if exists entry:
            for d in entry.documents:
                not exists d
            not exists entry
    ensures: RepositoryIssuesJob.created(repository: repository, action: remove, status: queued, queued_at: now)
}

-- A refresh request enqueues at most one pending code job per repository.
-- from: modules/indexer/code/indexer.go:307
rule QueueCodeIndexJob {
    when: CodeIndexRefreshRequested(repository)
    let service = code_search_service()
    requires: service.enabled
    requires: not exists CodeIndexJob{repository: repository, status: queued}
    ensures: CodeIndexJob.created(repository: repository, status: queued, queued_at: now)
}

-- Bring the repository's index in line with its default-branch head.
-- Repositories whose kind is not listed in config.repo_indexer_repo_types
-- (black box repository_kind_indexed) are skipped:
-- forks, mirrors and templates each need their kind listed; anything else
-- counts as a source repository. The first indexing, or a head that no
-- longer descends from the indexed commit (force push), rebuilds the
-- repository's documents from scratch; otherwise only added, modified,
-- renamed and deleted paths are touched.
-- from: modules/indexer/code/indexer.go:44
rule CodeIndexJobRuns {
    when: job: CodeIndexJob.queued_at <= now
    requires: job.status = queued
    requires: code_search_service().status = ready
    let repository = job.repository
    let head = default_branch_head(repository)
    let entry = CodeIndexEntry{repository: repository}
    ensures:
        if not repository_kind_indexed(repository):
            job.status = skipped
        else:
            job.status = completed
            if exists entry:
                entry.commit_sha = head
                entry.indexed_at = now
            else:
                CodeIndexEntry.created(
                    service: code_search_service(),
                    repository: repository,
                    commit_sha: head,
                    indexed_at: now
                )
            CodeIndexRefreshed(repository: repository, commit_sha: head)
    @guidance
        -- Documents after the job are exactly the files of `head` for which
        -- is_indexable_file(path, size) holds (see invariant
        -- CodeIndexMirrorsDefaultBranch). Files above max_indexer_file_size
        -- are removed from the index; non-text files keep only their path;
        -- content is converted to UTF-8 dropping invalid bytes; the
        -- language is detected from name and content.
        -- A job that fails (indexer error, git error) stays queued and is
        -- retried; an indexer that is not ready fails every job.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Language statistics refresh
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: modules/indexer/stats/indexer.go
rule QueueLanguageStatsJob {
    when: LanguageStatsRefreshQueued(repository)
    requires: not exists LanguageStatsJob{repository: repository, status: queued}
    ensures: LanguageStatsJob.created(repository: repository, status: queued, queued_at: now)
}

-- Empty repositories and repositories whose default-branch head was already
-- measured are skipped; otherwise repositories recomputes the statistics.
-- from: modules/indexer/stats/db.go:29
rule LanguageStatsJobRuns {
    when: job: LanguageStatsJob.queued_at <= now
    requires: job.status = queued
    let repository = job.repository
    let head = default_branch_head(repository)
    let mark = LanguageStatsMark{repository: repository}
    ensures:
        if repository.is_empty:
            job.status = skipped
        else if exists mark and mark.commit_sha = head:
            job.status = skipped
        else:
            job.status = completed
            if exists mark:
                mark.commit_sha = head
            else:
                LanguageStatsMark.created(repository: repository, commit_sha: head)
            LanguageStatsComputed(repository: repository, commit_sha: head, sizes: language_sizes(repository, head))
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Issue index maintenance
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: modules/indexer/issues/indexer.go:65
rule IssueIndexerStarts {
    when: IssueIndexerStartupCompleted(service, index_was_empty)
    requires: service.status = starting
    ensures: service.status = ready
    ensures:
        if index_was_empty:
            IssueIndexRebuildStarted(service: service)
}

-- from: modules/indexer/issues/indexer.go:147
rule IssueIndexerStartupTimesOut {
    when: service: IssueIndexService.started_at + config.indexer_startup_timeout <= now
    requires: service.status = starting
    ensures: service.status = unavailable
    ensures: IndexerStartupFailed(kind: service.kind)
}

rule IssueIndexerBecomesUnreachable {
    when: IssueIndexerHealthChanged(service, reachable)
    requires: service.status = ready
    requires: not reachable
    ensures: service.status = unavailable
}

rule IssueIndexerRecovers {
    when: IssueIndexerHealthChanged(service, reachable)
    requires: service.status = unavailable
    requires: reachable
    ensures: service.status = ready
}

-- A full rebuild walks every repository and re-queues all of its issues.
-- from: modules/indexer/issues/indexer.go:221
rule IssueIndexRebuildQueuesEverything {
    when: IssueIndexRebuildStarted(service)
    ensures: service.last_full_rebuild_at = now
    ensures:
        for repository in all_repositories():
            RepositoryIssuesReindexRequested(repository: repository)
}

-- Scheduled full rebuild (cron task `rebuild_issue_indexer`, off by default).
-- from: services/cron/tasks_extended.go:210
rule ScheduledIssueIndexRebuild {
    when: service: IssueIndexService.last_full_rebuild_at + config.rebuild_issue_indexer_interval <= now
    requires: config.rebuild_issue_indexer_enabled
    requires: service.status = ready
    ensures: IssueIndexRebuildStarted(service: service)
}

-- The administration cron task `rebuild_issue_indexer` (timer or "run now")
-- starts the same full rebuild as the schedule above.
-- from: services/cron/tasks_extended.go:210
rule IssueIndexRebuildTaskRuns {
    when: administration/IssueIndexRebuildDue()
    requires: issue_index_service().status = ready
    ensures: IssueIndexRebuildStarted(service: issue_index_service())
}

-- Newly created repositories (including generated-from-template and forks)
-- get their issues indexed (templates may carry issues).
-- from: modules/repository/create.go:305
rule CreatedRepositoryIssuesIndexed {
    when: repositories/RepositoryCreated(repository, doer)
    ensures: RepositoryIssuesReindexRequested(repository: repository)
}

-- The public/private flag of every issue document follows its repository.
-- from: modules/repository/create.go:303
rule VisibilityChangeReindexesIssues {
    when: repositories/RepositoryVisibilityChanged(repository, doer)
    ensures: RepositoryIssuesReindexRequested(repository: repository)
}

rule QueueRepositoryIssuesJob {
    when: RepositoryIssuesReindexRequested(repository)
    requires: not exists RepositoryIssuesJob{repository: repository, action: reindex, status: queued}
    ensures: RepositoryIssuesJob.created(repository: repository, action: reindex, status: queued, queued_at: now)
}

-- Re-queue every issue of the repository, or drop all of its documents.
-- from: modules/indexer/issues/util.go:132
rule RepositoryIssuesJobRuns {
    when: job: RepositoryIssuesJob.queued_at <= now
    requires: job.status = queued
    ensures: job.status = drained
    ensures:
        if job.action = reindex:
            for issue in issues_of(job.repository):
                IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
        else:
            for d in issue_documents_of(job.repository):
                not exists d
}

-- Every event that changes an indexed field of an issue re-indexes it
-- (title, body, comments, state, labels, milestone, assignees, reviews,
-- review requests, merge).
-- from: services/indexer/notify.go:38
rule IssueOpenedIsIndexed {
    when: issues/IssueOpened(issue, mentions)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule IssueClosedIsReindexed {
    when: issues/IssueClosed(issue, doer, comment)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule IssueReopenedIsReindexed {
    when: issues/IssueReopened(issue, doer, comment)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule IssueTitleChangeIsReindexed {
    when: issues/IssueTitleChanged(issue, doer, old_title)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule IssueContentChangeIsReindexed {
    when: issues/IssueContentChanged(issue, doer, old_content)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule IssueRefChangeIsReindexed {
    when: issues/IssueRefChanged(issue, doer, old_ref)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule IssueLabelsChangeIsReindexed {
    when: issues/IssueLabelsChanged(issue, doer, added, removed)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule IssueLabelsClearIsReindexed {
    when: issues/IssueLabelsCleared(issue, doer)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule IssueMilestoneChangeIsReindexed {
    when: issues/IssueMilestoneChanged(issue, doer, old_milestone)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule IssueAssigneeChangeIsReindexed {
    when: issues/IssueAssigneeChanged(issue, doer, assignee, removed, comment)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule CommentCreatedReindexesIssue {
    when: issues/IssueCommentCreated(issue, comment, doer, mentions)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: issue)
}

rule CommentEditedReindexesIssue {
    when: issues/IssueCommentEdited(comment, doer, old_content)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: comment.issue)
}

rule CommentDeletedReindexesIssue {
    when: issues/IssueCommentDeleted(comment, doer)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: comment.issue)
}

rule PullRequestOpenedIsIndexed {
    when: pulls/PullRequestOpened(pull_request)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: pull_request.issue)
}

rule PullRequestMergedIsReindexed {
    when: pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: pull_request.issue)
}

rule PullRequestAutoMergedIsReindexed {
    when: pulls/PullRequestAutoMerged(pull_request, merger)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: pull_request.issue)
}

rule ReviewSubmittedReindexesPull {
    when: pulls/ReviewSubmitted(review)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: review.pull_request.issue)
}

rule ReviewRequestedReindexesPull {
    when: pulls/ReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, reviewer)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: pull_request.issue)
}

rule ReviewRequestRemovedReindexesPull {
    when: pulls/ReviewRequestRemoved(pull_request, doer, reviewer)
    ensures: IssueReindexRequested(issue: pull_request.issue)
}

-- from: services/indexer/notify.go:88
rule DeletedIssueLeavesIndex {
    when: issues/IssueDeleted(issue, doer)
    requires: not exists IssueIndexJob{issue: issue, action: remove, status: queued}
    ensures: IssueIndexJob.created(issue: issue, action: remove, status: queued, queued_at: now)
}

rule QueueIssueJob {
    when: IssueReindexRequested(issue)
    requires: not exists IssueIndexJob{issue: issue, action: index, status: queued}
    ensures: IssueIndexJob.created(issue: issue, action: index, status: queued, queued_at: now)
}

-- Rebuild the document from the issue's current state; an issue that no
-- longer exists (or a remove job) drops the document.
-- from: modules/indexer/issues/indexer.go:173
rule IssueJobRuns {
    when: job: IssueIndexJob.queued_at <= now
    requires: job.status = queued
    requires: issue_index_service().status = ready
    let issue = job.issue
    let doc = IssueIndexDocument{issue: issue}
    ensures: job.status = drained
    ensures:
        if exists doc:
            not exists doc
        if job.action = index:
            IssueIndexDocument.created(
                service: issue_index_service(),
                issue: issue,
                repository: issue.repository,
                is_public: not issue.repository.is_private,
                title: issue.title,
                content: issue_body(issue),
                comments: issue_comment_texts(issue),
                is_pull: issue.is_pull,
                is_closed: issue.status = closed,
                labels: issue_labels(issue),
                milestone: issue_milestone(issue),
                project: issue_project(issue),
                project_column: issue_project_column(issue),
                poster: issue.poster,
                assignees: issue_assignees(issue),
                mentioned: issue_mentions(issue),
                reviewed_by: issue_reviewers(issue),
                review_requested: issue_requested_reviewers(issue),
                subscribers: issue_subscribers(issue),
                created_at: issue_created_at(issue),
                updated_at: issue_updated_at(issue),
                deadline: issue_deadline(issue),
                comment_count: issue_comment_texts(issue).count
            )
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Re-index requests
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Site admins can force a repository to be re-indexed.
-- from: routers/web/repo/setting/setting.go:790
rule AdminRequestsCodeReindex {
    when: AdminRequestsReindex(admin, repository, kind)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: kind = code
    requires: code_search_service().enabled
    ensures: CodeIndexRefreshRequested(repository: repository)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{owner}/{repo}/settings action=admin_index
        --   request_reindex_type=code|stats|issues. Code re-index without an
        --   indexer is forbidden.
}

rule AdminRequestsStatsReindex {
    when: AdminRequestsReindex(admin, repository, kind)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: kind = stats
    ensures: LanguageStatsRefreshQueued(repository: repository)
}

rule AdminRequestsIssuesReindex {
    when: AdminRequestsReindex(admin, repository, kind)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: kind = issues
    ensures: RepositoryIssuesReindexRequested(repository: repository)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Issue and pull-request search
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The query language of the keyword box (all scopes):
--   word        should-match term, fuzzy
--   +word       must match;   -word   must not match
--   "a phrase"  exact (non-fuzzy) term; backslash escapes + - \ "
--   is:open | is:closed | -is:open | -is:closed | is:all   state filter
--   sort:created|updated|comments|deadline:asc|desc  (anything else: relevance)
--   modified:>YYYY-MM-DD | modified:<YYYY-MM-DD | modified:YYYY-MM-DD
--   author:NAME  assignee:NAME  review:NAME  mentions:NAME  (unknown names ignored)
-- If no term carries + or -, all plain terms become must-match.
-- Terms match title, body and conversation comments.
--
-- An empty keyword lists straight from the issue store (never from the
-- index), so an issue created a moment ago always appears in plain lists.
-- from: modules/indexer/issues/indexer.go:333
rule ReaderListsRepositoryIssues {
    when: ReaderListsRepositoryIssues(viewer, repository, kind, involvement, keyword, state, sort)
    requires: kind != both
    requires: kind = issues_only implies can_read_issues(viewer, repository)
    requires: kind = pulls_only implies can_read_pulls(viewer, repository)
    requires: involvement = all or viewer != null
    requires: not contains_nul(keyword)
    let service = issue_index_service()
    ensures: IssueSearch.created(
        viewer: viewer,
        scope: repository,
        repository: repository,
        keyword: keyword,
        tokens: parse_issue_query(keyword),
        kind: kind,
        state: state,
        involvement: involvement,
        no_label_only: false,
        no_milestone_only: false,
        no_assignee_only: false,
        include_all_public: false,
        searchable_repositories: { repository },
        sort: sort,
        page: 1,
        page_size: config.issue_page_size,
        used_index: keyword != "",
        index_unavailable: keyword != "" and service.status != ready,
        results: issue_search(viewer, { repository }, keyword, kind, state, involvement, sort),
        open_count: issue_search_count(viewer, { repository }, keyword, kind, open, involvement),
        closed_count: issue_search_count(viewer, { repository }, keyword, kind, closed, involvement)
    )
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{owner}/{repo}/issues and /pulls (q, type=all|
        --   your_repositories|assigned|created_by|mentioned|review_requested|
        --   reviewed_by, state=open|closed|all, labels=1,-2 (include/exclude,
        --   0 = no label), milestone (-1 = none), project, assignee (-1 =
        --   none), poster, sort, page); GET /{owner}/{repo}/issues/search
        --   (JSON for pickers); API GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues with
        --   state, labels, q, type, milestones, since, before, created_by,
        --   assigned_by, mentioned_by.
        -- Default sort: latest (newest first). When the index is unavailable
        -- a keyword search shows a warning instead of results.
}

-- The signed-in user's cross-repository dashboards (/issues, /pulls) and
-- organization dashboards (/org/{org}/issues|pulls, optionally per team).
-- Searchable repositories: those the context owner owns or the viewer
-- collaborates on (organization: the org's repositories the viewer can
-- read, restricted to the team's when a team is selected), excluding
-- archived repositories and repositories with the unit disabled. On their
-- own dashboard, for every filter except your_repositories, issues in any
-- public repository also count.
-- from: routers/web/user/home.go:374
rule UserViewsPersonalIssueDashboard {
    when: UserViewsIssueDashboard(viewer, context_org, context_team, kind, involvement, keyword, state, sort)
    requires: viewer != null
    requires: viewer.is_active
    requires: kind != both
    requires: context_org = null
    requires: context_team = null
    let repos = dashboard_repositories(viewer, context_org, context_team, kind)
    let all_public = involvement != your_repositories
    let service = issue_index_service()
    ensures: IssueSearch.created(
        viewer: viewer,
        scope: dashboard,
        context_owner: viewer,
        context_org: context_org,
        context_team: context_team,
        keyword: keyword,
        tokens: parse_issue_query(keyword),
        kind: kind,
        state: state,
        involvement: involvement,
        no_label_only: false,
        no_milestone_only: false,
        no_assignee_only: false,
        include_all_public: all_public,
        searchable_repositories: repos,
        sort: sort,
        page: 1,
        page_size: config.issue_page_size,
        used_index: keyword != "",
        index_unavailable: keyword != "" and service.status != ready,
        results: issue_search(viewer, repos, keyword, kind, state, involvement, sort),
        open_count: issue_search_count(viewer, repos, keyword, kind, open, involvement),
        closed_count: issue_search_count(viewer, repos, keyword, kind, closed, involvement)
    )
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /issues, /pulls (signed-in only), GET /org/{org}/issues,
        --   /org/{org}/pulls, /org/{org}/issues/{team} …; parameters q, type,
        --   state, labels (organization labels only on org dashboards),
        --   project, milestone, assignee, sort (default recent_update), page.
        -- Default involvement: created_by on the personal dashboard,
        --   your_repositories on organization dashboards.
        -- Pull request rows carry approval / change-request / waiting
        --   review counts and the head's combined commit status.
}

rule UserViewsOrganizationIssueDashboard {
    when: UserViewsIssueDashboard(viewer, context_org, context_team, kind, involvement, keyword, state, sort)
    requires: viewer != null
    requires: viewer.is_active
    requires: kind != both
    requires: context_org != null
    requires: is_org_member(viewer, context_org) or viewer.is_admin
    let repos = dashboard_repositories(viewer, context_org, context_team, kind)
    let service = issue_index_service()
    ensures: IssueSearch.created(
        viewer: viewer,
        scope: organization,
        context_owner: viewer,
        context_org: context_org,
        context_team: context_team,
        keyword: keyword,
        tokens: parse_issue_query(keyword),
        kind: kind,
        state: state,
        involvement: involvement,
        no_label_only: false,
        no_milestone_only: false,
        no_assignee_only: false,
        include_all_public: false,
        searchable_repositories: repos,
        sort: sort,
        page: 1,
        page_size: config.issue_page_size,
        used_index: keyword != "",
        index_unavailable: keyword != "" and service.status != ready,
        results: issue_search(viewer, repos, keyword, kind, state, involvement, sort),
        open_count: issue_search_count(viewer, repos, keyword, kind, open, involvement),
        closed_count: issue_search_count(viewer, repos, keyword, kind, closed, involvement)
    )
    @guidance
        -- Same parameters as the personal dashboard; organization labels are
        -- offered as filters; default involvement is your_repositories.
}

-- REST /repos/issues/search across everything the client can see.
-- from: routers/api/v1/repo/issue.go:35
rule ClientSearchesIssues {
    when: ClientSearchesIssues(client, keyword, kind, state, involvement, owner, team, sort)
    requires: team = null or owner != null
    requires: involvement != your_repositories
    requires: involvement = all or client != null
    let repos = api_issue_search_repositories(client, owner, team)
    let service = issue_index_service()
    ensures: IssueSearch.created(
        viewer: client,
        scope: api,
        context_owner: owner,
        context_team: team,
        keyword: keyword,
        tokens: parse_issue_query(keyword),
        kind: kind,
        state: state,
        involvement: involvement,
        no_label_only: false,
        no_milestone_only: false,
        no_assignee_only: false,
        include_all_public: owner = null,
        searchable_repositories: repos,
        sort: sort,
        page: 1,
        page_size: config.api_default_page_size,
        used_index: keyword != "",
        index_unavailable: keyword != "" and service.status != ready,
        results: issue_search(client, repos, keyword, kind, state, involvement, sort),
        open_count: issue_search_count(client, repos, keyword, kind, open, involvement),
        closed_count: issue_search_count(client, repos, keyword, kind, closed, involvement)
    )
    @guidance
        -- API: GET /api/v1/repos/issues/search (state=open|closed|all
        --   default open, labels and milestones by name — unknown names
        --   discarded, q, priority_repo_id, type=issues|pulls, since, before,
        --   assigned, created, mentioned, review_requested, reviewed, owner,
        --   team (requires owner), page, limit, sort default latest).
        -- Unknown owner or team: rejected as a bad request.
        -- A token limited to public resources searches public repositories only.
}

-- from: routers/web/user/home.go:145
rule UserViewsMilestonesDashboard {
    when: UserViewsMilestonesDashboard(viewer, context_org, keyword, show_closed)
    requires: viewer != null
    requires: directory().milestones_dashboard_enabled
    requires: context_org = null or is_org_member(viewer, context_org) or viewer.is_admin
    let repos = dashboard_repositories(viewer, context_org, null, issues_only)
    ensures: MilestoneOverview.created(
        viewer: viewer,
        context_org: context_org,
        keyword: keyword,
        show_closed: show_closed,
        repositories: repos,
        milestones: milestone_search(repos, keyword, show_closed)
    )
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /milestones, /org/{org}/milestones[/{team}] (repos,
        --   q, state, sort=nearduedate|furthestduedate|leastcomplete|
        --   mostcomplete|mostissues|leastissues). Only repositories with
        --   at least one milestone and the issues unit readable are listed.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Autocomplete
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Users offered for @-mentions: participants of the issue (or none on a new
-- issue) plus users assignable in the repository. Teams are offered only in
-- organization repositories: every team for org owners and site admins,
-- otherwise the viewer's own teams. Entries render as "org/team".
-- from: routers/web/repo/issue.go:3793
rule WriterRequestsMentionCandidates {
    when: WriterRequestsMentionCandidates(viewer, repository, issue)
    requires: can_read_issues(viewer, repository) or can_read_pulls(viewer, repository)
    ensures: MentionCandidates.created(
        viewer: viewer,
        repository: repository,
        issue: issue,
        users: mentionable_users(repository, issue),
        teams: mentionable_teams(viewer, repository)
    )
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Insights
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Pulse. Each section appears only if the viewer can read its unit; the code
-- section also needs a non-empty repository. Merged = merged within the
-- period; proposed = still-open PRs created within the period; opened /
-- closed issues by creation / closing time; unresolved = open issues
-- created before the period but updated within it; releases = non-draft
-- releases created within it. Code statistics cover the default branch
-- (commit_count_all_branches covers all branches).
-- from: routers/web/repo/activity.go:21
rule ReaderViewsActivity {
    when: ReaderViewsActivity(viewer, repository, period)
    let can_code = can_read_code(viewer, repository)
    let can_issues = can_read_issues(viewer, repository)
    let can_pulls = can_read_pulls(viewer, repository)
    let can_releases = can_read_releases(viewer, repository)
    requires: can_code or can_issues or can_pulls or can_releases
    let from = now - period_length(period)
    let has_code = can_code and not repository.is_empty
    ensures:
        let report = ActivityReport.created(
            viewer: viewer,
            repository: repository,
            period: period,
            from: from,
            until: now,
            includes_releases: can_releases,
            includes_issues: can_issues,
            includes_pulls: can_pulls,
            includes_code: has_code,
            merged_pulls: merged_pulls_since(repository, from),
            opened_pulls: opened_pulls_since(repository, from),
            opened_issues: opened_issues_since(repository, from),
            closed_issues: closed_issues_since(repository, from),
            unresolved_issues: unresolved_since(repository, from, can_issues, can_pulls),
            published_releases: releases_since(repository, from),
            code: code_activity(repository, from),
            top_authors: top_authors(repository, from, config.activity_top_authors)
        )
        if not can_pulls:
            report.merged_pulls = {}
            report.opened_pulls = {}
        if not can_issues:
            report.opened_issues = {}
            report.closed_issues = {}
        if not can_releases:
            report.published_releases = {}
        if not has_code:
            report.code = null
            report.top_authors = []
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{owner}/{repo}/activity[/{period}] with period one of
        --   daily (24h), halfweekly (72h), weekly (7d, the default and the
        --   fallback for unknown values), monthly, quarterly, semiyearly,
        --   yearly (calendar months/years).
        -- GET /{owner}/{repo}/activity_author_data[/{period}]: the top
        --   committers JSON (all branches), needs code read and a non-empty
        --   repository.
}

-- The contributors graph, code frequency and recent commits views all read
-- the same per-revision statistics (non-merge commits of the revision's
-- history, by author, per week). First request starts generation and asks
-- the client to come back.
-- from: services/repository/contributors_graph.go:84
rule ReaderRequestsContributorStats {
    when: ReaderRequestsContributorStats(viewer, repository, revision)
    requires: can_read_code(viewer, repository)
    requires: not repository.is_empty
    requires: not exists ContributorStats{repository: repository, revision: revision}
    ensures: ContributorStats.created(
        repository: repository,
        revision: revision,
        status: generating,
        requested_at: now
    )
    ensures: ContributorStatsGenerationStarted(repository: repository, revision: revision)
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{owner}/{repo}/activity/contributors[/data],
        --   /activity/code-frequency[/data], /activity/recent-commits[/data].
        --   While generating (or when another request is already generating
        --   the same revision) the data endpoints answer "accepted, retry".
}

-- from: services/repository/contributors_graph.go:230
rule ContributorStatsComplete {
    when: ContributorStatsGenerated(stats, succeeded)
    requires: stats.status = generating
    requires: succeeded
    ensures: stats.status = ready
    ensures: stats.series = contributor_series(stats.repository, stats.revision)
    ensures: stats.generated_at = now
    ensures: stats.expires_at = now + config.contributor_stats_ttl
}

-- A failed generation is remembered (served as an error) until it expires.
rule ContributorStatsFail {
    when: ContributorStatsGenerated(stats, succeeded)
    requires: stats.status = generating
    requires: not succeeded
    ensures: stats.status = failed
    ensures: stats.expires_at = now + config.contributor_stats_ttl
}

-- Cached statistics are discarded after the cache TTL; the next request
-- regenerates them.
-- from: services/repository/contributors_graph.go:311
rule ContributorStatsExpire {
    when: stats: ContributorStats.expires_at <= now
    requires: stats.status in { ready, failed }
    ensures: not exists stats
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Profiles
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A profile is shown only to viewers who may see the account. Without a
-- usable profile README the overview tab shows repositories. The README is
-- read from the default branch of the subject's `.profile` repository, and
-- only when that repository is not a fork, not private, not empty and its
-- code is readable by the viewer. Listings on every tab are filtered by what
-- the viewer may see; private repositories appear only to signed-in viewers
-- with access.
-- from: routers/web/user/profile.go:60
rule ViewerOpensProfile {
    when: ViewerOpensProfile(viewer, subject, tab)
    requires: can_see_profile(viewer, subject)
    let readme = has_profile_readme(subject, viewer)
    ensures:
        let view = ProfileView.created(
            viewer: viewer,
            subject: subject,
            requested_tab: tab,
            tab: tab,
            has_profile_readme: readme,
            shows_private: viewer != null and (viewer.is_admin or viewer = subject),
            repositories: profile_repositories(viewer, subject, tab, readme),
            people: profile_people(viewer, subject, tab),
            total: profile_total(viewer, subject, tab, readme)
        )
        if tab = overview and not readme:
            view.tab = repositories
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{username}?tab=overview|repositories|stars|watching|
        --   followers|following (+ q, sort, language, topic, archived, fork,
        --   mirror, template, private, page). Followers/following lists use
        --   profile_repo_page_size. Stars tab is absent when stars are
        --   disabled instance-wide. The activity/feed tabs belong to
        --   notifications/federation. Funding links from the profile
        --   repository are shown with the overview.
        -- No pinned repositories exist in Forgejo.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Crawlers: sitemap, robots
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The sitemap index lists one sitemap page per sitemap_page_size public
-- active individual users (unless the users page is disabled) and per
-- sitemap_page_size repositories visible to the requester.
-- from: routers/web/home.go:92
rule CrawlerFetchesSitemapIndex {
    when: CrawlerFetchesSitemapIndex(requester)
    let dir = directory()
    requires: dir.sitemap_enabled
    requires: requester != null or not (dir.require_signin_view or dir.explore_require_signin)
    ensures: SitemapDocument.created(
        is_index: true,
        page: 1,
        entry_count: sitemap_page_count(requester, users) + sitemap_page_count(requester, repositories)
    )
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /sitemap.xml.
}

-- A sitemap page lists profile / repository URLs with their last update.
-- from: routers/web/explore/repo.go:111
rule CrawlerFetchesSitemapPage {
    when: CrawlerFetchesSitemapPage(requester, section, page)
    let dir = directory()
    requires: dir.sitemap_enabled
    requires: requester != null or not (dir.require_signin_view or dir.explore_require_signin)
    requires: section != users or not dir.users_page_disabled
    requires: page >= 1
    ensures: SitemapDocument.created(
        is_index: false,
        section: section,
        page: page,
        entry_count: sitemap_entries(requester, section, page, config.sitemap_page_size).count
    )
    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /explore/repos/sitemap-{n}.xml, /explore/users/sitemap-{n}.xml.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- go get
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Answered for any path with ?go-get=1, whether or not the repository
-- exists or the requester may read it, so that the go tool can proceed to
-- authenticate on clone. The branch used for source links is the
-- repository's default branch when it exists, else the instance default.
-- from: routers/web/goget.go:20
rule GoToolRequestsImportMeta {
    when: GoToolRequestsImportMeta(requester, owner_name, repo_name)
    requires: owner_name != ""
    requires: trim_git_suffix(repo_name) != ""
    let repository = repository_named(owner_name, repo_name)
    ensures: GoImportAnswer.created(
        owner_name: owner_name,
        repo_name: repo_name,
        import_path: go_import_path(owner_name, trim_git_suffix(repo_name)),
        clone_url: clone_url(owner_name, repo_name, config.go_get_clone_url_protocol),
        source_branch: if repository != null: repository.default_branch else: config.default_branch_name,
        insecure_hint: instance_is_plain_http()
    )
    @guidance
        -- Any GET /{owner}/{repo}[/...]?go-get=1. Response carries
        --   go-import "<import> git <clone_url>" and go-source "<import> _
        --   <src/branch/BRANCH>{/dir} <src/branch/BRANCH>{/dir}/{file}#L{line}"
        --   plus a "go get [--insecure] <import>" hint. Missing owner or
        --   repo name: "invalid import path".
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Markup rendering (misc API)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Renders text the way the instance renders it in issues, files and wikis.
-- In `comment` mode with a repository, issue references and mentions are
-- resolved against that repository; other modes render as a document.
-- Relative links resolve against `context_path` (made absolute under the
-- instance URL unless already an http(s) URL).
-- from: routers/api/v1/misc/markup.go:19
rule ClientRendersMarkup {
    when: ClientRendersMarkup(client, mode, text, context_path, file_path, is_wiki, repository)
    requires: client != null
    requires: mode != file or renderer_exists_for(file_path)
    requires: repository = null or can_see_repository(client, repository)
    ensures: MarkupRendering.created(
        requester: client,
        mode: mode,
        text: text,
        context_path: context_path,
        file_path: file_path,
        is_wiki: is_wiki,
        repository: repository,
        html: if text = "": "" else: sanitize(render_markup(mode, text, context_path, file_path, is_wiki, repository))
    )
    @guidance
        -- API: POST /api/v1/markup {Mode, Text, Context, FilePath,
        --   BranchPath, Wiki}; POST /api/v1/markdown {Mode, Text, Context,
        --   Wiki}; POST /api/v1/markdown/raw (body is the markdown);
        --   POST /api/v1/repos/{owner}/{repo}/markup|markdown|markdown/raw
        --   (repository context). All require an authenticated client.
        -- Web: POST /-/markup and /{owner}/{repo}/markup (previews).
        -- Unknown mode or unsupported file extension: unprocessable.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Search never reveals a repository the viewer cannot read.
invariant RepositorySearchShowsOnlyReadable {
    for s in RepositorySearches:
        for r in s.results:
            can_see_repository(s.viewer, r)
}

-- Facets are honoured exactly.
invariant RepositorySearchHonoursFacets {
    for s in RepositorySearches:
        for r in s.results:
            (archived in s.facets implies r.is_archived)
            and (not_archived in s.facets implies not r.is_archived)
            and (fork in s.facets implies r.is_fork)
            and (not_fork in s.facets implies not r.is_fork)
            and (mirror in s.facets implies r.is_mirror)
            and (not_mirror in s.facets implies not r.is_mirror)
            and (template in s.facets implies r.is_template)
            and (not_template in s.facets implies not r.is_template)
            and (private in s.facets implies r.is_private)
            and (public in s.facets implies not r.is_private)
            and (relevant_only in s.facets implies not r.is_empty)
}

invariant RepositorySearchPageBounded {
    for s in RepositorySearches:
        s.results.count <= s.page_size
}

-- Users and organizations listed are ones the viewer may see.
invariant UserSearchShowsOnlyListable {
    for s in UserSearches:
        for u in s.results:
            listable_account(u, s.viewer)
}

invariant ExploreAndPickerListOnlyActiveUsers {
    for s in UserSearches:
        for u in s.results:
            s.scope != api implies u.is_active
}

invariant OrganizationSearchShowsOnlyListable {
    for s in OrganizationSearches:
        for o in s.results:
            listable_organization(o, s.viewer)
}

-- Code hits come only from repositories whose code the viewer can read.
invariant CodeHitsReadable {
    for h in CodeSearchHits:
        can_read_code(h.search.viewer, h.repository)
}

-- Issue results are readable, and pull requests appear only under the pull
-- request unit's permission.
invariant IssueResultsReadable {
    for s in IssueSearches:
        for i in s.results:
            (i.is_pull implies can_read_pulls(s.viewer, i.repository))
            and (not i.is_pull implies can_read_issues(s.viewer, i.repository))
}

invariant IssueResultsMatchState {
    for s in IssueSearches:
        for i in s.results:
            (s.state = open implies i.status = open)
            and (s.state = closed implies i.status = closed)
}

invariant IssueResultsMatchKind {
    for s in IssueSearches:
        for i in s.results:
            (s.kind = issues_only implies not i.is_pull)
            and (s.kind = pulls_only implies i.is_pull)
}

invariant IssueResultsWithinSearchableRepositories {
    for s in IssueSearches:
        for i in s.results:
            i.repository in s.searchable_repositories
                or (s.include_all_public and not i.repository.is_private)
}

-- One code index entry per repository; one document per path per entry.
invariant OneCodeIndexEntryPerRepository {
    for a in CodeIndexEntries:
        for b in CodeIndexEntries:
            (a != b) implies a.repository != b.repository
}

invariant OneIssueDocumentPerIssue {
    for a in IssueIndexDocuments:
        for b in IssueIndexDocuments:
            (a != b) implies a.issue != b.issue
}

-- The public flag of an issue document always follows its repository once
-- pending jobs have drained.
invariant IssueDocumentVisibilityFollowsRepository {
    for d in IssueIndexDocuments:
        (not exists IssueIndexJob{issue: d.issue, action: index, status: queued})
            implies d.is_public = not d.repository.is_private
}

-- The queues never hold two pending jobs for the same work.
invariant CodeIndexQueueIsUnique {
    for a in CodeIndexJobs:
        for b in CodeIndexJobs:
            (a != b and a.status = queued and b.status = queued)
                implies a.repository != b.repository
}

invariant LanguageStatsQueueIsUnique {
    for a in LanguageStatsJobs:
        for b in LanguageStatsJobs:
            (a != b and a.status = queued and b.status = queued)
                implies a.repository != b.repository
}

invariant IssueIndexQueueIsUnique {
    for a in IssueIndexJobs:
        for b in IssueIndexJobs:
            (a != b and a.status = queued and b.status = queued and a.action = b.action)
                implies a.issue != b.issue
}

invariant RepositoryIssuesQueueIsUnique {
    for a in RepositoryIssuesJobs:
        for b in RepositoryIssuesJobs:
            (a != b and a.status = queued and b.status = queued and a.action = b.action)
                implies a.repository != b.repository
}

-- Only default-branch content, of eligible files, is ever indexed.
invariant CodeIndexMirrorsDefaultBranch {
    for d in CodeIndexDocuments:
        file_at(d.entry.repository, d.entry.commit_sha, d.path)
            and is_indexable_path(d.path)
}

invariant OneContributorStatsPerRevision {
    for a in ContributorStatses:
        for b in ContributorStatses:
            (a != b) implies (a.repository != b.repository or a.revision != b.revision)
}

invariant TopAuthorsBounded {
    for r in ActivityReports:
        r.top_authors.count <= config.activity_top_authors
}

-- A report never includes a section the viewer cannot read.
invariant ActivitySectionsRespectUnits {
    for r in ActivityReports:
        (not r.includes_pulls implies (r.merged_pulls.count = 0 and r.opened_pulls.count = 0))
        and (not r.includes_issues implies (r.opened_issues.count = 0 and r.closed_issues.count = 0))
        and (not r.includes_releases implies r.published_releases.count = 0)
        and (not r.includes_code implies r.code = null)
}

-- Rendered markup is always sanitised.
invariant RenderedMarkupIsSanitised {
    for m in MarkupRenderings:
        is_sanitised(m.html)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Signed-in users and site administrators are the shared actors
-- access/SignedInUser and access/SiteAdmin.

-- An account that can read a given repository's code.
actor RepositoryReader {
    within: repositories/Repository
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_read_code(this, within)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The explore area as seen by anyone (anonymous visitors are represented by
-- a null viewer in the triggers). Restricted users see only what they have
-- been explicitly given; anonymous visitors see only public repositories of
-- public owners.
surface ExploreDirectory {
    facing visitor: accounts/User

    context search: RepositorySearch where viewer = visitor

    exposes:
        search.keyword
        search.sort
        search.facets
        search.total
        for r in search.results:
            r.name
            r.is_archived
            r.is_fork
            r.is_mirror
            r.is_template
            r.is_private

    provides:
        ViewerSearchesRepositories(visitor, scope, subject, keyword, language, facets, sort)
        ViewerSearchesUsers(visitor, scope, keyword, sort)
        ViewerExploresOrganizations(visitor, keyword, sort)
        ViewerSearchesAllCode(visitor, keyword, language, path, mode)
        ClientSearchesTopics(visitor, keyword)

    @guarantee ExploreRespectsSignInRequirement
        -- When the instance or the explore area requires sign-in, anonymous
        -- requests to every explore page, the sitemap, the user search API
        -- and the user picker are refused (redirect to sign-in / 401).
    @guarantee DisabledPagesRedirect
        -- A disabled users, organizations or code page redirects to the
        -- repositories page; the repositories page cannot be disabled.
    @guidance
        -- GET /explore -> /explore/repos. Repository rows show owner,
        -- name, description (sanitised), topics, primary language, stars,
        -- forks, last update, and archived/fork/mirror/template/private
        -- badges; the language filter lists primary languages.
}

surface UserDirectory {
    facing visitor: accounts/User

    context search: UserSearch where viewer = visitor

    exposes:
        search.keyword
        search.total
        for u in search.results:
            u.name
            u.visibility

    provides:
        ViewerSearchesUsers(visitor, scope, keyword, sort)

    @guarantee EmailOnlyWhenAllowed
        -- Email addresses are shown on explore only when SHOW_USER_EMAIL is
        -- on, the viewer is signed in and the address is not kept private
        -- (always for the viewer's own row and for site admins). Matching by
        -- email never matches a hidden address.
}

surface OrganizationDirectory {
    facing visitor: accounts/User

    context search: OrganizationSearch where viewer = visitor

    exposes:
        search.keyword
        search.total
        for o in search.results:
            o.name
            o.visibility

    provides:
        ViewerExploresOrganizations(visitor, keyword, sort)
}

surface CodeSearchPage {
    facing visitor: accounts/User

    context search: CodeSearch where viewer = visitor

    exposes:
        search.keyword
        search.effective_mode
        search.used_index
        search.index_unavailable
        search.total
        search.languages
        for h in search.hits:
            h.repository.name
            h.path
            h.language
            h.lines

    provides:
        ViewerSearchesAllCode(visitor, keyword, language, path, mode)
        ViewerSearchesOwnerCode(visitor, owner, keyword, language, path, mode)
        ReaderSearchesRepositoryCode(visitor, repository, ref_name, keyword, path, mode)

    @guarantee ModesOffered
        -- With an indexer: exact, union, and fuzzy only when fuzzy is
        -- enabled. Without one: exact, union, regexp (repository scope only).
}

surface IssueSearchPage {
    facing visitor: accounts/User

    context search: IssueSearch where viewer = visitor

    exposes:
        search.keyword
        search.state
        search.kind
        search.involvement
        search.sort
        search.open_count
        search.closed_count
        search.index_unavailable
        for i in search.results:
            i.index
            i.title
            i.status
            i.is_pull
            i.repository.name

    provides:
        ReaderListsRepositoryIssues(visitor, repository, kind, involvement, keyword, state, sort)
        UserViewsIssueDashboard(visitor, context_org, context_team, kind, involvement, keyword, state, sort)
        ClientSearchesIssues(visitor, keyword, kind, state, involvement, owner, team, sort)
        UserViewsMilestonesDashboard(visitor, context_org, keyword, show_closed)

    @guarantee FreshListings
        -- Listing without a keyword reads the issue store directly, so an
        -- issue appears in lists as soon as it is created even if the index
        -- lags or is down.
}

surface RepositoryInsights {
    facing reader: accounts/User

    context report: ActivityReport where viewer = reader

    exposes:
        report.period
        report.from
        report.until
        report.active_pull_count
        report.active_issue_count
        report.merged_pulls
        report.opened_pulls
        report.opened_issues
        report.closed_issues
        report.unresolved_issues
        report.published_releases
        report.code
        report.top_authors

    provides:
        ReaderViewsActivity(reader, repository, period)
        ReaderRequestsContributorStats(reader, repository, revision)

    timeout:
        ContributorStatsExpire
}

surface ContributorGraphs {
    facing reader: RepositoryReader

    context repository: repositories/Repository

    let stats = ContributorStats{repository: repository, revision: repository.default_branch}

    exposes:
        stats.status
        stats.series when stats.status = ready
        stats.generated_at when stats.status = ready

    provides:
        ReaderRequestsContributorStats(reader, repository, revision)

    @guidance
        -- Contributors graph: per-contributor weekly commits with a
        -- selectable metric (commits / additions / deletions). Code
        -- frequency: weekly additions vs deletions of the "total" series.
        -- Recent commits: the last year of weekly commit counts.
}

surface ProfilePage {
    facing visitor: accounts/User

    context view: ProfileView where viewer = visitor

    exposes:
        view.subject.name
        view.tab
        view.has_profile_readme
        view.total
        for r in view.repositories:
            r.name
        for p in view.people:
            p.name

    provides:
        ViewerOpensProfile(visitor, subject, tab)
        ViewerSearchesOwnerCode(visitor, owner, keyword, language, path, mode)
}

surface ComposerAutocomplete {
    facing writer: access/SignedInUser

    context candidates: MentionCandidates where viewer = writer

    exposes:
        for u in candidates.users:
            u.name
        for t in candidates.teams:
            t.organization.name

    provides:
        WriterRequestsMentionCandidates(writer, repository, issue)
        ViewerSearchesUsers(writer, scope, keyword, sort)
        ClientSearchesTopics(writer, keyword)
}

surface Crawlers {
    facing crawler: accounts/User

    context dir: Directory

    exposes:
        dir.robots_policy
        dir.sitemap_enabled

    provides:
        CrawlerFetchesSitemapIndex(crawler)
        CrawlerFetchesSitemapPage(crawler, section, page)
        GoToolRequestsImportMeta(crawler, owner_name, repo_name)

    @guidance
        -- GET /robots.txt: the operator's custom file if present, else a
        --   default policy that disallows the API, avatars, user pages,
        --   explore query strings, repository create/migrate/fork, and
        --   per-repository source, blame, commit(s), raw, media, tags,
        --   graph, branches, compare, activity, actions, projects, labels,
        --   milestones, search, attachments, archives, .patch/.diff/.bundle,
        --   feeds, and any URL with lang=, redirect_to=, tab=, q=, sort=.
}

surface MiscellaneousApi {
    facing client: accounts/User

    context dir: Directory

    exposes:
        dir.version
        for t in all_templates():
            t.kind
            t.name

    provides:
        ClientRendersMarkup(client, mode, text, context_path, file_path, is_wiki, repository)
        ClientReadsTemplate(client, kind, name)
        ClientSearchesTopics(client, keyword)

    @guarantee SanitisedOutput
        -- Rendered HTML passes an allow-list sanitiser: no script, style
        -- elements or event-handler attributes; javascript:, vbscript: and
        -- data: links are removed (custom URL schemes may be allowed by the
        -- operator); only a fixed set of classes, a few data-* attributes
        -- and color/background-color styles survive; operator-defined
        -- sanitiser rules may extend the allow-list. External renderers
        -- may opt out per renderer (no_sanitizer) or be isolated in a
        -- sandboxed frame (iframe).
    @guidance
        -- API: GET /api/v1/version (public), GET /api/v1/settings/ui|api|
        --   attachment|repository (public summaries of instance settings,
        --   owned by administration), the template listings and markup
        --   endpoints listed on the rules.
}

surface ReindexControls {
    facing admin: access/SiteAdmin

    context repository: repositories/Repository

    let entry = CodeIndexEntry{repository: repository}

    exposes:
        entry.commit_sha
        entry.indexed_at

    provides:
        AdminRequestsReindex(admin, repository, kind)

    @guidance
        -- Shown in repository settings to site admins only: the commit the
        -- code index and language statistics last reflected, and buttons to
        -- re-index code (only with an indexer), stats and issues.
}

-- The code index backend reporting on itself (start-up completion and
-- health), as seen by the rest of the system.
surface CodeIndexBackend {
    facing backend: CodeSearchService

    exposes:
        backend.kind
        backend.status
        backend.fuzzy_enabled

    provides:
        CodeIndexerStartupCompleted(backend, index_was_empty)
        CodeIndexerHealthChanged(backend, reachable)

    timeout:
        CodeIndexerStartupTimesOut
}

surface IssueIndexBackend {
    facing backend: IssueIndexService

    exposes:
        backend.kind
        backend.status
        backend.last_full_rebuild_at

    provides:
        IssueIndexerStartupCompleted(backend, index_was_empty)
        IssueIndexerHealthChanged(backend, reachable)

    timeout:
        IssueIndexerStartupTimesOut
        ScheduledIssueIndexRebuild
}

-- The background generator of contributor statistics.
surface ContributorStatsWorker {
    facing job: ContributorStats

    exposes:
        job.repository.name
        job.revision
        job.status

    provides:
        ContributorStatsGenerated(job, succeeded)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred Markup.render       -- see: markup.allium (renderers, link/mention/issue-ref processing, sanitiser allow-list)
deferred CodeIndexer.query   -- see: implementation note; per-backend tokenisation and scoring
deferred IssueIndexer.query  -- see: implementation note; per-backend scoring for relevance sort

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "go-get answers reveal a private repository's default branch name to anyone; should the answer for unreadable repositories use the instance default branch instead?"
open question "User search hides private accounts from everyone but admins/self/org co-members, while profile visibility also admits followers of a private account; should the two rules be unified?"
open question "The API user search is disabled whenever the explore users page is disabled, which also breaks pickers that use the API; should the API stay available to signed-in users?"
open question "An indexer that does not become ready within STARTUP_TIMEOUT terminates the instance; should a rebuild degrade to 'search unavailable' instead?"
open question "Instance-wide code search for site admins searches every repository, including private ones they have no role in; intended?"
open question "Explore orders by recent update by default but profile tabs fall back to the explore default too; should profiles have their own default sort?"
open question "Only conversation comments are indexed for issue search; should review (code) comments be searchable too?"
open question "The relevant-only filter treats 'has avatar' as relevance; keep that heuristic?"

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQUEST access: confirm the local predicates map onto AuthorizationPolicy (can_read, has_any_access, can_see_profile, can_see_owner_user); explore's anonymous/limited/restricted listing rule must equal has_any_access.
-- REQUEST accounts/User.keep_email_private, full_name, last_login_at, created_at, updated_at: user search matching and sort orders.
-- REQUEST organizations: a membership predicate (is_org_member) usable for org dashboards and organization listings.
-- REQUEST repositories/Repository.description, has_avatar, topics, primary_language, num_stars, num_forks, size, git_size, lfs_size, updated_at, created_at: keyword match, facets and sort orders.
-- REQUEST repositories/Topic.name, repositories/Topic.repo_count: topic search orders by usage.
-- REQUEST repositories: RecordLanguageStats should treat LanguageStatsComputed as emitted by discovery's stats job (it already listens for it).
-- REQUEST code: mirror syncs must also emit CommitsPushed for default-branch changes so mirrors are re-indexed.
-- REQUEST issues/Issue.content, created_at, updated_at, deadline, labels, assignees, milestone, mentions, subscribers, project: the indexed projection (read here via black-box accessors issue_*).
-- REQUEST pulls: reviewer sets per pull request (reviewed_by, review_requested) for the index projection.
